    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "From stocking stores to supporting customer requests, we rely on frontline workers’ labor daily. Yet, many remain stuck in low-wage, precarious jobs despite having the motivation to move up the career ladder. A key impediment is a lack of understanding of the competencies required to land their target jobs. Co-designed with industry professionals, Braintrust enables learners to try their target jobs’ day-to-day tasks. The learners’ submissions are compared to outputs developed by practitioners of the target jobs, enabling learners to self-assess their strengths and weaknesses. By tapping into this braintrust of experts, frontline workers gain clarity around which learning experiences to prioritize as they pursue their future jobs.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Lam, B. (2024). Braintrust. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/vv903bj4056. https://doi.org/10.25740/vv903bj4056.",
